## Discipline gate - READ BEFORE ANY CODE CHANGE

**Do not make code changes without an active task spec** at `.agent/tasks/<id>.md`.
The spec is the contract: proceed within its `files.touched`, and write
`.agent/verifications/<id>.md` when done. A pre-commit hook on `agent/*` branches
rejects commits without the spec. Bypass with `--no-verify` only when the operator
has waived it. If the operator's direction is ambiguous ("go", "make X work"), ask
for the task spec first.

## Session-start protocol

1. Read [docs/CURRENT_STATE.md](docs/CURRENT_STATE.md).
2. Drift check: its `## As of` entry against `git log --oneline -1`. Fix the doc first.
3. Verify the build: `py -3.12 -m pytest -q` passes.
4. Verify git is clean: `git status --short`.
5. Ask the operator which task to work on.

